>Kannel</surname><given-names>WB</given-names></name><name><surname>Dawber</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>High density lipoprotein as a protective factor against coronary heart disease</article-title><source>Am J Med</source><year>1977</year><volume>62</volume><fpage>707</fpage><lpage>714</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">193398</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0002-9343(77)90874-9</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Van Lenten</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hama</surname><given-names>SY</given-names></name><name><surname>deBeer</surname><given-names>FC</given-names></name><name><surname>Stafforini</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>McIntyre</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><name><surname>Prescott</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Anti-inflammatory HDL becomes pro-inflammatory during the acute phase response</article-title><source>J Clin Invest</source><year>1995</year><volume>96</volume><fpage>2758</fpage><lpage>2767</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8675645</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1172/JCI118345</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Navab</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hama</surname><given-names>SY</given-names></name><name><surname>Hough</surname><given-names>GP</given-names></name><name><surname>Subbanagounder</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Reddy</surname><given-names>ST</given-names></name><name><surname>Fogelman</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A cell-free assay for detecting HDL that is dysfunctional in preventing the formation of or inactivating oxidized phospholipids</article-title><source>J Lipid Res</source><y